  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on minimizing the probability of the worst outcome (0 Euros), which is 99.8% for A and 99.9% for B—so A is preferred. The individual’s reasoning aligns with this in outcome (favoring A due to lower chance of loss), but the focus in the verbal report is on the higher winning probability (0.2% vs 0.1%) rather than explicitly on the lower probability of the minimum outcome. However, since the probability of the minimum outcome is complementary to the winning probability (i.e., 1 - P(win) = P(loss)), the two perspectives are mathematically equivalent in this binary-outcome context. The individual does not explicitly mention the 99.8% or 99.9% loss probabilities but refers to the higher winning chance and lower risk of A, which reflects the same underlying comparison. Therefore, although the reasoning is expressed in terms of winning chances and perceived risk, it is consistent with the logic of the decision reason. The individual likely used a rule that coincides with the decision reason, even if not articulated in identical terms.",
